### ============================================================
### LogiRed API — Pruebas funcionales interactivas
### Compatible con: IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client
### ============================================================
### USO:
###   1. Levantar la app localmente (./mvnw spring-boot:run)
###   2. Ejecutar cada request en orden
###   3. El token JWT se captura automaticamente tras el login
### ============================================================

# Variables globales
@baseUrl       = http://localhost:8080
@adminEmail    = admin@logired.com
@adminPassword = Admin1234!
@authToken     = <PENDIENTE — ejecutar "1. Login Admin" primero>


### ============================================================
### SEGURIDAD — Autenticacion
### ============================================================

### 1. Login de Administrador (captura el token JWT)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### — IntelliJ: descomenta el bloque siguiente para captura automatica de token
# > {%
#   client.global.set("authToken", response.body.token);
#   client.log("Token JWT capturado: " + response.body.token);
# %}


### ============================================================
### SEGURIDAD — Registro de usuarios
### ============================================================

### 2a. Registro de usuario con rol COMERCIO
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "Comercio Nuevo",
  "email": "nuevocomer@logired.com",
  "password": "Comercio1234!",
  "rol": "COMERCIO"
}

###

### 2b. Registro de usuario con rol REPARTIDOR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "Repartidor Test",
  "email": "repartidor@logired.com",
  "password": "Repartidor1234!",
  "rol": "REPARTIDOR"
}

###

### 3. Login de Comercio (obtener token propio)
# @name loginComercio
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "comercio@logired.com",
  "password": "Comercio1234!"
}

### — IntelliJ: descomenta para captura automatica
# > {%
#   client.global.set("authToken", response.body.token);
# %}


### ============================================================
### COMERCIOS — CRUD (requiere JWT)
### ============================================================

### 4. Listar todos los comercios
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/comercios
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 4b. Obtener comercio por ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/comercios/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 4c. Registrar un nuevo Comercio
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/comercios
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "nombre": "Sushi Express",
  "direccion": "Av. Santa Fe 3000, CABA",
  "telefono": "1198765432",
  "email": "sushi@logired.com"
}

###

### 4d. Eliminar un comercio
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/comercios/99
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


### ============================================================
### PEDIDOS — CRUD completo (requiere JWT)
### ============================================================

### 5. Crear un nuevo Pedido
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/pedidos
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "comercioId": 1,
  "direccionDestino": "Av. Rivadavia 5000, CABA"
}

###

### 6a. Listar todos los pedidos
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/pedidos
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 6b. Obtener pedido por ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/pedidos/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 6c. Listar pedidos por comercio
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/pedidos/comercio/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 6d. Listar pedidos por estado
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/pedidos/estado/CREADO
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 7. Actualizar estado de un pedido (CREADO → EN_CAMINO)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/pedidos/1/estado
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "estado": "EN_CAMINO"
}

###

### 8. Cancelar un pedido
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/pedidos/1/cancelar
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


### ============================================================
### PRUEBAS DE SEGURIDAD — Acceso sin token (deben dar 401/403)
### ============================================================

### 9a. GET /api/pedidos sin token → debe dar 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/pedidos

###

### 9b. POST /api/pedidos sin token → debe dar 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/pedidos
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "comercioId": 1,
  "direccionDestino": "Test sin auth"
}

###

### 9c. GET /api/comercios sin token → debe dar 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/comercios
